-- title:
--   Original Gaussian finitecap stepped coefficients have integrable time squares and covariance
-- statement:
--   The original stopped clipped-gradient coefficient K on either finite deterministic mesh is a measurable bounded finite step process. Its squared and mixed products are integrable in the original probability space for each time, and their expected values are integrable across the finite deterministic horizon.
-- source:
--   True essential child of the original physical two-grid L2 integrability package gb92 bd2d25a4-b1d8-4944-8bbc-788e37995514. Its proof uses the exact original Gaussian process and unchanged original stopping assumptions.

import Mathlib
